<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Fed's absense in the market was in line with forecasts by Wall Street economists.</p>
<p>Seven-day fixed system repurchase agreements carried out by the Fed on Thursday are perceived to be enough to carry the central bank through the weekend, analysts said.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the time when the Fed usually intervenes in the market, the federal funds rate was at 5-3/16 percent, below the central bank's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676</p>
